        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Bulge</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">16 December 1944 to 25 January 1945</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a> region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a>, with fighting at Elsenborn Ridge, St. Vith and Bastogne</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> under Hitler, with Army Group B under Walter Model and OB West under Gerd von Rundstedt, who committed over 410,000 men, just over 1,400 tanks and armoured fighting vehicles, 2,600 artillery pieces and over 1,000 combat aircraft; the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Dwight D. Eisenhower</a>, whose forces eventually numbered more than 700,000 men</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The German offensive was halted short of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> and broken by 27 December, and the front line was effectively restored to its pre-attack position by the end of January. Casualties are put at between 63,000 and 104,000 for the Germans and 77,000 to more than 83,000 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>.</span></div>
